        area that feels like you've landed on another planet. This excursion
        takes us to the Gorafe desert, one of the most surprising landscapes in
        southern Spain, located in the heart of the Granada Geopark (UNESCO), a
        desert area with ravines, dried-up rivers, and rugged mountain
        landscapes in badlands and high plateaus. The route winds over dusty
        gravel roads, alternated with singletracks and dry plateaus, along
        cliffs, erosion gullies, and dry riverbeds formed millions of years ago.
      </p>
